{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6961001","formula":"C₂₁H₂₅NO₄","hill":"C21H25NO4","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":25.0,"N":1.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Nalmexone"},"descriptions":{"en":"Nalmexone (INN; also known as nalmexone hydrochloride (USAN) or by the development codes EN-1620A and UM-592) is a semisynthetic, opioid partial agonist or mixed agonist-antagonist with both analgesic and narcotic antagonist properties that was never marketed. In clinical studies it was found to have comparable analgesic efficacy to morphine, though with several-fold reduced potency. In addition, nalmexone's side effects, the most common of which were sleepiness and sweating, were reported to be similar to those of morphine, albeit with a noticeably higher degree of incidence."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":5360516,"mass":355.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(=CCN1CC[C@]23[C@@H]4C(=O)CC[C@]2([C@H]1CC5=C3C(=C(C=C5)O)O4)O)C","inchikey":"OHKCLOQPSLQCQR-MBPVOVBZSA-N","iupac":"(4R,4aS,7aR,12bS)-4a,9-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enyl)-2,4,5,6,7a,13-hexahydro-1H-4,12-methanobenzofuro[3,2-e]isoquinolin-7-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5360516","atoms":51,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.654,"y":-0.355,"z":-1.602,"el":"O"},{"x":0.232,"y":2.855,"z":-0.106,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.304,"y":1.502,"z":-0.529,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.681,"y":-3.005,"z":-0.921,"el":"O"},{"x":2.04,"y":0.808,"z":0.305,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.727,"y":0.677,"z":-0.569,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.263,"y":1.658,"z":0.518,"el":"C"},{"x":0.919,"y":0.957,"z":1.27,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.071,"y":0.944,"z":-1.265,"el":"C"},{"x":0.424,"y":0.433,"z":-1.574,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.104,"y":-0.622,"z":0.056,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.423,"y":2.098,"z":1.429,"el":"C"},{"x":0.476,"y":-0.382,"z":1.961,"el":"C"},{"x":1.725,"y":-0.004,"z":-0.874,"el":"C"},{